ential assumptions and uncertainties\\nAssumptions listed in `assumptions[]` and uncertainties (with priority flags) in `uncertainties[]`.\\n\\nRecommend resolving **U1, U2, U4, U5** before the formal design is locked; U3, U6, U7 preferred; U8, U9 informational.\\n\", \"evidence\": \"Repository inspection: `ls -la /workspace` \\u2192 only `task.json` present; no `track.md` file on disk (the field in task.json is metadata stating it is design-only). Python 3.12.3 available; 24 CPU cores; ~125 GiB RAM; ~775 GiB free. Network disabled, no GPU, no torch/transformers/peft/trl/vllm, no HF auth tokens. `task.json` confirms research question: \\\"Will BAdam achieve better performance on zero-shot math benchmarks compared to LoRA when finetuning the Llama 3-70B model on the MathInstruct dataset?\\\" with explicit \\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\\\" and \\\"Do not claim that an experiment was run.\\\"\", \"assumptions\": [\"A1. Subject model is Llama-3-70B base (non-Instruct) in bf16, since using Instruct would bias both methods similarly and conflict with MathInstruct's purpose.\", \"A2. BAdam uses 10 blocks across 80 layers (8 layers/block), cyclic rotation with 1-epoch warmup before rotation starts; AdamW(beta=(0.9,0.999), wd=0); peak LR tuned in {1e-5, 2e-5, 5e-5} per method.\", \"A3. LoRA primary config: r=32, alpha=64, dropout=0.05, all-linear targets; fp32 adapters, bf16 frozen base; AdamW.\", \"A4. MathInstruct = TIGER-Lab/MathInstruct released train split; primary condition uses a stratified 50-80K subsample preserving source proportions; 1-2K held-out for dev.\", \"A5. Evaluation panel: GSM8K + MATH are primary metrics; SVAMP + AQuA-RAT are secondary.\", \"A6. Decoding is greedy, temperature=0, max_new_tokens 512 for MATH and 256 for others; single canonical prompt template across seeds/methods.\", \"A7. Contamination threshold: drop test items with >=25-gram overlap or full-string match to MathInstruct train before scoring.\", \"A8. n_seeds=5; paired t-test with Holm-Bonferroni over 4 benchmarks; Cohen's d_z and 10000-iter BCa bootstrap CI reported.\", \"A9. Primary comparison cell = LoRA(r=32, all-linear) vs BAdam-Block-LoRA(r chosen to match param budget); BAdam-Full as a secondary cell. Subject to researcher confirmation via U2.\", \"A10. Cosine LR schedule, warmup ratio 0.03, weight decay 0, identical across cells; identical seed-initialised token stream shared between paired cells.\"], \"uncertainties\": [\"U1 [HIGH]. Subject model choice: Llama-3-70B base vs 70B-Instruct vs 70B-base with chat template. Must resolve before locking design.\", \"U2 [HIGH]. Which BAdam variant is 'the BAdam baseline' against LoRA: BAdam-Full (headline memory-efficient full-parameter) vs BAdam-Block-LoRA (LoRA-inside-active-block). Recommended: include both cells.\", \"U3 [MEDIUM]. Exact BAdam paper hyperparameters (block count, rotation schedule, warmup length, optimizer betas, offload choice). Recommend confirm against Luo et al. 2024.\", \"U4 [HIGH]. MathInstruct exact version and HuggingFace path/hash; released set has multiple re-shares.\", \"U5 [HIGH]. Acceptance criterion for 'better': strict superiority (Delta>0 with corrected p<0.05 on >=1 primary) vs non-inferiority within a 1pp margin vs Pareto (accuracy vs peak memory). Determines required n_seeds and testing budget.\", \"U6 [MEDIUM]. Benchmark contamination mitigation: drop >=25-gram-overlap items, and whether AQuA/SVAMP \\u2014 which overlap MathInstruct sources \\u2014 are included as benchmark.\", \"U7 [MEDIUM]. Hardware & memory budget (H100/A100 count and interconnect), which determines feasibility of BAdam-Full within the question's scope.\", \"U8 [LOW]. Llama-3-70B license/gated-access \\u2014 assumed granted for design-only purposes.\", \"U9 [LOW]. Llama-3 tokenizer & prompt template lock-in (base model has new BPE but no chat tokens by default).\"]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-e2a96d72-0ec5-427f-98af-a7b7e3e24