{"id": "b4392eec-9839-4db9-a9fe-a02b34fa24f8", "timestamp": "2026-10-20T23:19:20.598864", "source": "user", "parent_id": "64d60c51-eac8-462f-a6b2-041a5491354e", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Approach approved. The plan you proposed is well-scoped for a design-only deliverable: clear operationalization, sound alignment logic (matched params + matched tokens + matched wall-clock), defensible primary benchmarks (GSM8K, MATH) with sensible secondaries (SVAMP, AQuA-RAT), and a rigorous paired statistical plan with Holm-Bonferroni, Cohen's d_z and BCa bootstrap CI. Resolving the open questions before you write the final design document so we lock these as defaults (not assumptions): (1) Subject model = **Llama-3-70B base (non-Instruct) in bf16**. Cleaner attribution — any instruction-following observed is attributable to MathInstruct SFT; using Instruct would confound both arms equally and defeat the purpose of the fine-tune (concern U1). (2) BAdam variants — design **both** cells: **(a) primary cell = LoRA(r=32, α=64, all-linear) vs BAdam-Full** with the headline block-wise memory-optimized full-parameter SFT (this is what the BAdam paper actually proposes and is the spirit of the BAdam-vs-LoRA question, treated as 'same compute envelope, different parameterization'), and **(b) fairness-mirror secondary cell = LoRA(r=32) vs BAdam-Block-LoRA** with r chosen to match LoRA's trainable scalar parameter count within 2× (resolves U2 directly). (3) Dataset = TIGER-Lab/MathInstruct standard release train split (262K); primary condition uses a **stratified 80K subsample preserving the 13 source proportions**; hold out 2K for dev. Full 262K is a scale-robustness condition (resolves U4). (4) Acceptance criterion (resolves U5) — report **three framings explicitly** so the conclusion is not cherry-picked from a single test: (i) **superiority** (paired t-test/Wilcoxon, Δ = mean(BAdam) − mean(LoRA) > 0 with Holm-corrected p<0.05 on ≥1 primary benchmark); (ii) **non-inferiority** within a **1.0 percentage-point margin** (|Δ| ≤ 1pp with corrected p>0.05 on both primary benchmarks; 1pp justified by typical 5-seed paired std LoRA@r=32 reports); (iii) **Pareto** accuracy-vs-peak-memory, with peak GPU memory reported per cell. The headline question is answered against all three. (5) Hardware feasibility block (resolves U7) — state the assumed envelope as **2–4× H100/H200 80GB with NVLink and ZeRO-3 + activation checkpointing + bf16**; flag the BAdam-Full cell as requiring the upper bound (3–4× H100) for 1×70B in bf16 with full AdamW state, and document a documented-fallback **3 seeds** if budget is constrained. (6) Contamination gate (U6): keep the 25-gram + full-string-match drop rule, but **exclude AQuA-RAT from primary analyses if contamination rate exceeds 2%**; SVAMP is similarly audited. (7) Hyperparameter defaults from BAdam paper (U3): **10 blocks, cyclic rotation, 1-epoch warmup before rotation, AdamW(β=(0.9, 0.999), wd=0)**, peak LR tuned in {1e-5, 2e-5} per method and then frozen for the headline run. Now please produce the **final design document** as one consolidated deliverable, structured as: (A) Research question & operationalized hypotheses (with the three acceptance framings); (B) Materials — model, dataset, exact HF paths/versions, license/access notes, hardware assumption; (C) Methods — LoRA and BAdam-Full primary cells, BAdam-Block-LoRA fairness cell, alignment variables, locked hyperparameters, training schedule; (D) Evaluation — benchmark panel (primary/secondary), prompting, decoding, answer extraction, contamination gate; (E) Statistical analysis plan — seeds, pairing, tests, correction, effect sizes, CIs, pre-registration note; (F) Design matrix table — methods × configs × seeds × benchmark panel with cell counts; (G) Feasibility & costs — memory estimates per cell, GPU-hours estimate, mitigations; (H) Threats to validity — contamination, prompt sensitivity, single-model single-tokenizer, MathInduct source overlap with SVAMP/AQuA, seed variance; (I) Reporting plan — figure/table list and how the three framings map onto the headline answer; (J) References. Keep it design-only; do not invent or claim experimental results.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"result\", \"approach_approved\": true}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "kind": "MessageEvent", "source_event_index": 22}
